{"availability":"available","full":"flwfdd/TokenTour","name":"TokenTour","description":"「Token 之旅」交互式 LLM/Agent 教程","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-26T07:46:20Z","updated":"2026-08-19T02:50:59Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tokentour.flwfdd.xyz","topics":[],"demo":"https://tokentour.flwfdd.xyz/chat2token/playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:12:37.643Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:12:37.643Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:12:37.643Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:21.334Z","stars":9,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:40.918Z","stars":9,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:12:37.643Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A vertical cross-section of the LLM application stack—from Agent messages to tokens and KV cache.","LLM applications look simple from the outside, but a single turn passes through many layers: Agent messages, chat templates, tokenization, the context window, attention, and KV cache. Each layer has its own representation, and the connections between them are easy to lose.","TokenTour makes a vertical cut through that stack. Instead of explaining one layer in isolation, it follows the same conversation downward and shows how a change at one level propagates through the rest."],"features":["Messages → chat template: compare how model families such as Qwen3, DeepSeek-V3, and GPT-OSS serialize the same conversation and tool calls.","Text → tokens: inspect token boundaries, byte-level behavior, and how small edits change the sequence.","Tokens → context and KV cache: see causal attention, estimate KV memory, and visualize which prefix could be reused on the next turn.","Cross-layer tracing: hover or select an item to follow the corresponding region across the synchronized views."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flwfdd/TokenTour/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"15dfeca4cf746